 "notes": "Two branches meet at b16: (i) transformation -> retention (b11->b13), (ii) ROS/NO/ONOO- -> cytotoxicity (b10->b15). b10 (light-triggered reactive-species generation) has no fitting property_family (photochemical); typed PRP/value biological because it is read in cells. Retention (b13) is an in-vivo endpoint -> PRF/service_capability; TME markers explaining tumour kill -> MEC/pathway (r03 rule 18). o9->o10 (Pearson R computed from two registered CLSM channels) is a derives edge whose act is registration + pixel correlation; register_colocated_views used, see proposals. o3->o4 uses quantify_from_intensity on image ROI intensity (broadening proposed). Figures opened: F2, F3, F4, F5; F6 not opened (o18 figs left empty). b20 is an inferred audit: F2e-g compares light vs dark TRFC only; irradiated TKFC/TRF were not imaged, so rod-driven retention and PDT-induced vessel permeation are confounded.",
